e=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br>// You can include R code blocks in C++ files processed with sourceCpp<br>// (useful for testing and development). The R code will be automatically <br>// run after the compilation.<br>//</font></span></div><div>/*** R<br>timesTwo(42)<br>*/<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\"></span></div></code></div><div><br>Then running using sourceCpp function to run, I can run the Rcpp function successfully:</div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\"><table style=\"border:currentColor;width:1241px;color:rgb(0,0,0);text-transform:none;line-height:inherit!important;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;padding-bottom:8px;padding-left:6px;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;!important;font-size:10pt!important;font-style:inherit!important;font-variant:inherit!important;font-weight:inherit!important;word-spacing:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"line-height:1.2;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt!important;vertical-align:top\"><pre style=\"margin:0px;border:currentColor;line-height:1.2;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">Rcpp::sourceCpp(&#39;test_timesTwo.cpp&#39;)\r\n</span>\r\n&gt; timesTwo(42)\r\n[1] 84\r\n</pre></td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"line-height:1.2;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt!important;vertical-align:top\"></td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"line-height:1.2;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt!important;vertical-align:top\"><table style=\"width:1241px\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td width=\"1\" height=\"\" align=\"left\" style=\"line-height:1.2;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-s